  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:30` checked each line's item **name** (`'Widget'`) against the SKU it was given (`'sku-1'`). They never matched, so nothing was removed. `Cart.add` already matches on the SKU, so the two methods disagreed.\n\n**Fix:** `remove` now compares `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Check:**\n- `shop/demo.py` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.\n- None of the existing tests cover `Cart.remove`, so they would have passed with or without this fix. I didn't add one; a short test there would catch this if it came back.",
